# Project Structure

Feature-based React app. Keep code in the right layer and follow existing folder patterns.

## Top-Level Layout

```
src/
├── app/          # Router, layouts, app-level wiring only
├── features/     # Domain modules (pomodoro, journals, auth, …)
├── shared/       # Cross-feature UI, hooks, constants, Supabase client
├── assets/       # Static files (SVGs, sounds, images)
└── styles/       # Global CSS (theme, variables, utilities)
```

## Feature Modules (`src/features/<name>/`)

Add new domain code inside the owning feature, not in `shared/` or `app/`.

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `pages/` | Route-level entry points (thin composition) |
| `components/` | Feature UI, one component per folder |
| `hooks/` | Feature-specific hooks; barrel-export via `index.ts` |
| `apis/` | Supabase / raw data access |
| `queries/` | TanStack Query hooks (call `apis/`) |
| `mutations/` | TanStack mutations |
| `store/` | Zustand stores |
| `constants/`, `utils/`, `types/`, `transformers/` | As needed |

Export the feature's public API from `features/<name>/index.ts` when other features need it.

## Component Conventions

- Folder per component: `ComponentName/index.jsx` or `index.tsx`
- Nest subcomponents: `TaskList/ListItem/index.jsx`
- Pages compose feature components; avoid business logic in `app/`

```jsx
// ✅ GOOD — page composes feature components
const Pomodoro = () => (
  <>
    <PomodoroDesktop />
    <PomodoroMobile />
  </>
);

// ❌ BAD — API calls or stores directly in app/router or layouts
```

## Imports

Always use the `@/` alias (`@/*` → `src/*`):

```ts
import { Button } from "@/shared/ui";
import { queryKeys } from "@/shared/constants";
import { useTasksQuery } from "@/features/pomodoro/queries";
```

- Shared UI primitives → `@/shared/ui`
- Routes, query keys, globals → `@/shared/constants`
- Cross-feature code → `@/features/<feature>/…`
- Do not reach into another feature's internal `components/` unless already established

## Shared Layer

Put code in `shared/` only when used by 2+ features:

- `shared/ui/` — reusable primitives (Button, Dialog, …)
- `shared/hooks/` — generic hooks (`useDocumentTitle`, `useIsMobile`)
- `shared/supabase/` — Supabase client and table names
- `shared/react-query/` — QueryClient setup

## File Types

Mixed JS/TS codebase. Prefer TypeScript for new hooks, types, and utilities; match the surrounding file when editing existing `.jsx` components.
